artifact.self_contained_problem:
Let $G=(V,E,\omega,\sigma)$ be a signed weighted social network on a finite set of agents $V$, where each ordered or unordered pair $(i,j)\in E$ carries a signed weight $\omega_{ij}\in\mathbb{R}$ (with $\sigma_{ij}=\operatorname{sgn}(\omega_{ij})\in\{-1,+1\}$ encoding friendly/antagonistic ties), and each agent $i\in V$ has an importance (or social-impact) value $r_i\ge 0$. For a triad $\{i,j,k\}\subseteq V$ with all three edges present, the classical structural-balance indicator is $b_{ijk}=\sigma_{ij}\sigma_{jk}\sigma_{ik}\in\{-1,+1\}$, declaring the triad balanced iff $b_{ijk}=+1$, and the classical balance measure of $G$ is the fraction of balanced triads
$$B(G)=\frac{\#\{\{i,j,k\}: b_{ijk}=+1\}}{\#\{\{i,j,k\}\subseteq V\text{ triadically closed}\}}.$$
This measure has three structural shortcomings when used as a proxy for the robustness of the organization:
(i) triads are scored independently, although each agent typically participates in many overlapping triads simultaneously;
(ii) the magnitudes $\omega_{ij}$ of the signed relations are ignored;
(iii) the importance/impact $r_i$ of the agents forming a triad is ignored.

Problem. Construct a balance functional $T:\mathcal{G}\to\mathbb{R}$ on signed weighted networks with agent importances such that:
(a) at the triad level there is a real-valued triad score $T_{ijk}$ that depends jointly on the signs $\sigma_{\cdot\cdot}$, the weights $\omega_{\cdot\cdot}$, and the agent importances $r_i,r_j,r_k$, and reduces to $b_{ijk}$ in the unweighted, equal-importance limit;
(b) the aggregation of $\{T_{ijk}\}$ into $T(G)$ accounts for the overlap of triads (the same agent or edge belonging to many triads) rather than treating triads as independent samples;
(c) $T(G)$ is consistent with classical balance on the appropriate degenerate limit and yields a meaningful quantification of the robustness of the organization.

Specify such a $T_{ijk}$ and aggregation rule, and prove that the resulting measure simultaneously remedies the three shortcomings above while preserving the qualitative content of structural balance.
